  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="35a9fc47-5e1a-5cb8-9973-92ce55ed2370" activityNameId="a6fb51d1-607b-5540-9836-9993ec9ee87f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural stone plate, cut, at regional storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural stone plate, cut, at regional storage
The drilling for the mining process is assumed to be done with compressed air, which is produced with electricity. The sawing is assumed to be accomplished with diamond wires. The diamond losses are not taken into account even though they might be significant as no data on diamond production is available. The dust emissions are estimated based on the losses (volume of granite with a density of 2?750 kg/m3) by cutting a plate with the geometry 0.5 * 0.5 * 0.03 m and a weight of 20 kg. It is assumed that 95% of the dust is bound in the cooling water.;
UUID: fa69ed43-cfc5-31f6-b8e8-76d63a6d5bd8
Includes the raw material granite, the mining, sawing and cooling, the transports within the mine and to the regional storage in Switzerland and the infrastructure (machines). No administration, wastewater, wear and spare parts are included. Dust is accounted for.
Location: For some exchanges RER- and GLO-modules are used as proxy
Technology: Typical technology for average Swiss production. Mining of boulders by direct separation from rock, whole to whole drilling, kerving wire saw, oxygen lance and water jet. Cutting by wire saw.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: See geography
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fa69ed43-cfc5-31f6-b8e8-76d63a6d5bd8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
